    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `cc00b664f`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`6fb3d55ce`). The author's gate is green on the tree of this head: the quick gate became a full batch run, because `camcraft-geometry` changes (1223 steps, 0 failed, clippy and the three example catalog suites included), and the light lane (7 steps). The gate ran with the base `issue/4025-kernel-region`; the merge of the side branch after it changed no file. The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and has `Refs #4178`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`.\n- The safety floor applies: this stage decides where the tool goes down into the stock. No old planner calls the new code; with the default switch the output is identical.\n- The PR changes the return type of `EntryPlanner::entry` to a verdict, and it changes the law suite to match (`standins.rs`, `l4_fallback.rs`, `l5_entry.rs`, `kit.rs`). Check that `check_l4` with the rule `needs_fallback` is not weaker than before.\n- The PR adds two functions to `camcraft-geometry` (`geo2d::arc_points`, `Region::holds_path`) with unit tests.\n- PR #4189 (the ring and row planners) is open at the same time. The two PRs change different files, but each adds lines to `lib.rs` and to `tests/laws.rs`. The PR that merges second takes a merge of the side branch.",
